n markers in invasive breast carcinoma. Methodological aspects and prognostic value in a series of 257 cases</article-title><source>Anticancer Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>3283</fpage><lpage>3288</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Anticancer Res||24|3283||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15510624</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cattoretti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Key</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Duchrow</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schluter</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Galle</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerdes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Monoclonal antibodies against recombinant parts of the Ki-67 antigen (MIB 1 and MIB 3) detect proliferating cells in microwave-processed formalin-fixed paraffin sections</article-title><source>J Pathol</source><year>1992</year><volume>168</volume><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>363</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Pathol||168|357||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1484317</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ceccarelli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Trere</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Santini</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Taffurelli</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Chieco</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Derenzini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>AgNORs in breast tumours</article-title><source>Micron</source><year>2000</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>149</lpa